rom-hamster (0.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * First stable release; feature-complete for the M1-M5 scope.
  * Platforms: 101 platform rules across five sections (extensions, arcade
    suffixes, media directories, media suffixes, archive extensions), with
    factory / system / user layering and config --explain source tracing.
  * Import: single ROMs, zip/7z/rar/tar archives, side media and DAT files;
    two-phase planning, cancel, crash resume, ambiguous-extension prompts,
    multi-disc grouping and duplicate detection.
  * Library: SQLite schema v1 with transactional writes, FTS5 search with a
    LIKE fallback, 13 filter dimensions, 4 sort orders, and a detail view
    with eight media groups and cached thumbnails.
  * Export: EmulationStation, ES-DE and Pegasus manifests generated from
    versioned templates.
  * CLI: init, import, dat, list, search, show, edit, delete, export, stats,
    config, help and version.
  * GUI: GTK 4 list and detail panes, drag-and-drop import, progress with
    cancellation, video preview through the media backend and explicit
    degradation when no backend is available.
  * i18n: English msgids with a complete Simplified Chinese catalog.
  * Packaging: rom-hamster, rom-hamster-gui and rom-hamster-data; conffiles
    under /etc/rom-hamster; private library directory; AppStream metadata;
    man pages; lintian clean.
  * CI: {gui, nogui, asan} x {ubuntu:24.04, debian:13} builds, plus package
    install, conffile upgrade and purge verification on both distributions.

 -- Zhou Xin <zhouxin312@qq.com>  Sat, 14 Nov 2026 22:00:00 +0800
